    "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE_NORMALIZATION_UNSTABLE",
    "CORRECTED_VERDICT_2026_05_29": "INCONCLUSIVE -> leans AGAINST the holographic claim. The pre-registered robustness gate ('the two independent gap-matched controls must AGREE') FAILED violently: the ferro gap-matched control dips SUB-unity (0.32-0.76, RESEMBLING holo, RMS only 0.081 from holo) while the rescaled gap-matched control blows up SUPER-unity (peaks 4.09). Two gap-matched non-critical controls on opposite sides of unity => the sqrt(purity) washout normalization is NOT a stable observable. ROOT CAUSE: the rescaled chain lambda(-sumX-0.5sumZZ) has a near-degenerate clustered low-lying spectrum, so its PURITY collapses far faster than its amplitude (purity=0.007 at beta=2 vs holo 0.30) even at MATCHED GAP; dividing a sizable amplitude by sqrt(tiny purity) gives the blow-up. So sqrt(purity) fails as a washout divisor whenever spectral DENSITY differs, not just gap. RAW (un-normalized) amplitude degradation: holo, ferro, and rescaled all degrade by SIMILAR large amounts (holo 0.052, ferro 0.031, rescaled 0.041 at beta=0.25 cold-normalized), while only the gap-1.60 paramagnet degrades LESS (0.196) because it is barely thermalized. => raw degradation tracks HOW THERMALIZED the state is (gap + spectral density), NOT criticality. The gap-matched non-critical ferro control degrades AS MUCH AS holo. This SUPPORTS the gap/thermalization-artifact hypothesis and does NOT rescue SIM-028. NET: HYP-024's 'beyond washout = holography' claim remains NOT established; the washout-normalized residual is normalization-dependent and a gap-matched non-critical chain reproduces the holo degradation in raw amplitude. SCRIPT BUG: verdict logic must require the two controls to AGREE (same side of unity) before any 'survives' conclusion, and must use a normalization-invariant comparison (raw amplitude at matched beta*Delta), not sqrt(purity).",
